# Three scales in one world. big is large beside large; small is small beside small, where the
# 1e-320 subnormal is lost into a normal neighbour; grain sits wholly inside the subnormals,
# where addition is exact and the two accumulation orders therefore agree.
# zero and unit carry the comparison values: --! out compares within 1e-9, which cannot tell a
# subnormal from 0, so the pins below are exact == against a declared column instead.
n 4
col big num 1e300 2e300 -3e300 1
col small num 1e-320 1e-300 -1e-300 0
col grain num 2.5e-323 5e-324 -2.5e-323 0
col zero num 0 0 0 0
col unit num 5e-324 5e-324 5e-324 5e-324
ja 巨大 big
ja 微小 small
ja 粒 grain
ja 零 zero
ja 単位 unit
